\description{
Jobs run PlasticDB's analyses on the server: DIAMOND searches of genes,
genomes and genome sets against PlasticDB's proteins, the matching of a
table of taxa, pathway mapping, HMM screens and taxonomy trees. They need
an API key (\code{plasticdb_client(api_key = )} or \code{PLASTICDB_API_KEY};
without one the functions signal \code{plasticdb_api_key_required} before
anything is sent). Reading a shared job (\code{\link[=job_shared]{job_shared()}}) needs none.
}
\details{
\code{submit_job()} submits a job by its server name and returns a
\code{plasticdb_job} at once; the typed helpers (\code{annotate_gene()},
\code{annotate_genome()}, \code{compare_genomes()}, \code{annotate_list()},
\code{pathway_analysis()}, \code{hmm_screen()}, \code{build_tree()}) name and document
each job type's parameters. Then \code{\link[=wait_job]{wait_job()}} polls until it finishes and
\code{\link[=job_results]{job_results()}} returns its results. \code{search_sequence()} is synchronous:
it searches one sequence now and returns the hits.

\strong{Inputs.} A FASTA input is a file path (plain or gzip), FASTA text (a
string starting with \code{>}, or a character vector of lines), a single line
of residues, raw bytes, or a \link[Biostrings:AAStringSet]{Biostrings::AAStringSet} /
\link[Biostrings:DNAStringSet]{Biostrings::DNAStringSet} (use \code{blast_type = "blastx"} for nucleotide
input). A taxa table is a path, text or a data frame (sent tab-separated,
with its column names as the header row). Text and sets are written to
temporary files; every upload is named after its contents (\code{.gz} exactly
when it is gzip), as the server expects.

\strong{Releases.} A pinned client (or \verb{release =}) runs the job against that
release's archived reference databases; a job type or option the release
cannot answer signals \code{plasticdb_release_unsupported_filter}.

\strong{Retries and idempotency.} Each submission is sent with an
\code{Idempotency-Key} header: \code{idempotency_key}, or a new UUID for each call,
and the same key on every retry of that call. The server keeps a key for
24 hours per user and answers a repeat with the job the first request
created (\code{job_replayed()} is then \code{TRUE}), so with an API key a submission
is retried like a read: on a timeout, a dropped connection or a 5xx. Pass
your own key when a script may be re-run after a crash: the re-run gets
the first job back instead of a duplicate. When the retries run out, the
error names the key to resubmit with (field \code{idempotency_key}). The same
key with a different request signals
\code{plasticdb_idempotency_key_reused}.

\strong{Limits.} Submissions are rate-limited (30 an hour); a 429 is waited
out when \code{Retry-After} is within \code{max_retry_wait}. A file over the size
limit, or more than 20 genomes, is \code{plasticdb_payload_too_large}.
}
